      "traceTextDiagram": "CLI Run Command Entry\n└── agentctl run \u003cskill\u003e invocation \u003c-- cmd/agentctl/cmd/run.go:57\n    ├── executor.PrepareJob(data) \u003c-- 1a\n    │   └── runservice.PrepareJob() \u003c-- internal/runservice/jobs.go:35\n    │       └── jobStore.FindOrPrepareSkillJob() \u003c-- 1b\n    │           └── jobs/store.FindOrPrepareSkillJob() \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/store.go:196\n    │               └── executor.FindOrPrepareSkillJob() \u003c-- 1c\n    │                   └── executor.prepareSkillJob() \u003c-- 1d\n    │                       ├── compute ArgsHash from input \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:148\n    │                       └── persist.FindOrInsertJob() \u003c-- 1e\n    │                           └── SQLite transaction \u003c-- internal/storage/jobs/persist/store.go:283\n    │                               ├── SELECT by args_hash \u003c-- 1f\n    │                               └── INSERT if not found \u003c-- 1g\n    └── handle duplicate or execute \u003c-- cmd/agentctl/cmd/run.go:136",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen running skills in agentctl, **duplicate executions waste time and resources**. If a user runs the same skill with identical input multiple times (e.g., retrying a failed command, or multiple processes invoking the same hook), the system should recognize this and reuse the previous result instead of re-executing. The **job preparation and deduplication system** solves this by computing a SHA256 hash of the skill name and input, then atomically checking if a job with that hash already exists before creating a new one [1a].\n\n## Details\n\n### Hash-Based Deduplication\n\nThe deduplication mechanism relies on **deterministic hashing** [1d]. When preparing a job, the system:\n\n1. **Marshals the skill arguments** into a canonical JSON format containing the skill name, input size, and SHA256 of the input content\n2. **Computes a SHA256 hash** of this canonical representation to create the `args_hash` field\n3. Uses this hash as the **deduplication key** for database lookups\n\nThis approach avoids storing large input payloads in the database while still enabling exact-match deduplication.\n\n### Atomic Find-or-Insert\n\nThe core deduplication logic uses a **SQLite transaction** to ensure atomicity [1e]. Within a single transaction, the system:\n\n1. **Queries for an existing job** by `args_hash` [1f]\n2. If found, returns the existing job with `isDuplicate=true`\n3. If not found, **inserts a new job record** [1g] and returns it with `isDuplicate=false`\n\nThis transaction-based approach prevents race conditions when multiple concurrent processes attempt to dedupe the same job.\n\n### Integration with CLI\n\nThe CLI run command [1a] invokes job preparation through multiple layers: runservice → job store → executor → persistence [1b, 1c, 1d]. This layered architecture separates concerns:\n\n- **Runservice** handles high-level execution flow and options (including the `--dedupe` flag)\n- **Job store** provides the public API for job operations\n- **Executor** implements the core preparation logic\n- **Persistence** manages SQLite transactions and state\n\nWhen a duplicate is detected, the system takes a **separate code path** that waits for the existing job to complete rather than re-executing the skill."
    },
