        {
          "id": "6g",
          "path": "internal/storage/trajectory/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 269,
          "lineContent": "result, err := s.db.ExecContext(ctx, `\nUPDATE trajectories SET\n\troot_request_id = ?, task_ids_json = ?, epic_id = ?, agent_role = ?, job_id = ?,\n\ttrace_id = ?, status = ?, summary = ?, artifact_digest = ?, outcome_json = ?, updated_at = ?, session_id = ?\nWHERE workspace_id = ? AND id = ?`,",
          "title": "Persist trajectory update to SQLite",
          "description": "Updates trajectory record with final status and metadata for optimization queries"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Trajectory Result Capture Flow\n├── CaptureResult() entry point \u003c-- internal/trajectorycapture/capture.go:273\n│   ├── Parse result envelope \u003c-- 6a\n│   ├── Determine event kind \u003c-- 6b\n│   │   └── (maps command to event type) \u003c-- internal/trajectorycapture/capture.go:283\n│   ├── Extract artifact digest \u003c-- 6c\n│   │   └── (from env.Data or meta.CASDigest) \u003c-- internal/trajectorycapture/capture.go:332\n│   ├── Build event metadata \u003c-- internal/trajectorycapture/capture.go:336\n│   │   └── (TraceID, JobID, TaskID, etc.)\n│   ├── Insert result event \u003c-- 6d\n│   │   └── store.InsertEvent() \u003c-- internal/trajectorycapture/capture.go:356\n│   │       └── s.db.ExecContext(INSERT) \u003c-- internal/storage/trajectory/store.go:609\n│   ├── Determine trajectory outcome \u003c-- 6e\n│   │   └── (StatusOK → ok, else → error) \u003c-- internal/trajectorycapture/capture.go:371\n│   └── Update trajectory status \u003c-- 6f\n│       └── store.UpdateTrajectory() \u003c-- internal/trajectorycapture/capture.go:378\n│           └── Persist to SQLite \u003c-- 6g\n│               └── s.db.ExecContext(UPDATE) \u003c-- internal/storage/trajectory/store.go:269\n└── Returns error or nil",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen running skills in agentctl, the system needs to capture **execution trajectories** for training and evaluating AI agents. A trajectory is a coherent record of what happened during a run: the user's request, the tools called, and the final result. This data feeds into optimization systems that learn from past executions.\n\nThe challenge is **capturing results at the right moment** with the right metadata. When a skill completes execution [5g], the system must record the outcome as a normalized event, extract any CAS artifact references, determine success/failure status, and update the trajectory record—all while maintaining correlation with the original job and user request.\n\n## Details\n\n**Result capture starts after skill execution** [6a]. The system receives the result envelope (JSON output from the skill) and parses it to extract status, command, and data fields. This envelope contains everything needed to understand what the skill produced.\n\n**Event kind mapping** [6b] determines how to classify this result. A `hooks/*` command becomes a `hook_result` event, while `todo/manage` operations map to `task_transition` or `review_request` events depending on the operation. Most skills produce `tool_result` events. This classification enables downstream queries to filter by event type.\n\n**Artifact extraction** [6c] checks if the result references content-addressed storage. Large outputs are stored in CAS and referenced by SHA256 digest rather than inlined. The system looks in `env.Data.artifact` or `env.Meta.CASDigest` to find these references, which get stored in the event's `data_artifact` field.\n\n**Event insertion** [6d] creates a `trajectory_events` record with inline summary data (truncated for preview), the artifact digest if present, and correlation metadata (trace ID, job ID, task ID). This event becomes part of the trajectory's timeline, queryable by kind, timestamp, or correlation IDs.\n\n**Status propagation** [6e] maps the envelope's status field to trajectory status. `StatusOK` becomes `trajectory.StatusOK`, while errors become `trajectory.StatusError`. The system also extracts the summary text from the result data to populate the trajectory's summary field.\n\n**Trajectory update** [6f] persists the final state. The `UpdateTrajectory` call [6g] writes the status, summary, and any newly discovered task IDs back to the `trajectories` table. This makes the trajectory queryable by outcome for optimization purposes—successful runs can be retrieved as training examples.\n\nThe entire flow is **best-effort and non-blocking**. If trajectory capture fails, the skill result still gets returned to the user. Trajectory data enriches the system but doesn't block primary execution paths."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Maps the integration of job preparation with SHA256-based deduplication and parallel trajectory capture for training data collection. Key flows: CLI entry at [1a], atomic find-or-insert at [1f], trajectory initialization at [2a], duplicate handling at [4c], and result capture at [6d].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph CLI[\"CLI Entry\"]\n        1a[\"1a: executeRunCommand\u003cbr/\u003einvokes PrepareJob\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph JobPrep[\"Job Preparation Hub\"]\n        1b[\"1b: Runservice.PrepareJob\u003cbr/\u003edelegates to job store\"]\n        1c[\"1c: JobStore.FindOrPrepareSkillJob\u003cbr/\u003eforwards to executor\"]\n        1d[\"1d: Executor.FindOrPrepareSkillJob\u003cbr/\u003ecore preparation logic\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph JobDedupe[\"Job Dedupe Path\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Executor.prepareSkillJob\u003cbr/\u003ecalls find-or-insert\"]\n        1f[\"1f: Persist.FindOrInsertJob\u003cbr/\u003equeries by args_hash\"]\n        1g[\"1g: Persist.FindOrInsertJob\u003cbr/\u003einserts if not found\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph HashComp[\"Hash Computation\"]\n        3a[\"3a: Executor creates job\u003cbr/\u003ecomputes args hash\"]\n        3b[\"3b: ComputeSkillArgsHash\u003cbr/\u003eentry point\"]\n        3c[\"3c: MarshalSkillArgs\u003cbr/\u003ecanonical JSON\"]\n        3d[\"3d: SHA256 input bytes\u003cbr/\u003econtent addressing\"]\n        3e[\"3e: SHA256 final digest\u003cbr/\u003ecombines command + args\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph TrajInit[\"Trajectory Initialization\"]\n        2a[\"2a: PrepareJob initiates\u003cbr/\u003etrajectory capture start\"]\n        2b[\"2b: trajectorycapture.Start\u003cbr/\u003eopens trajectory store\"]\n        2c[\"2c: Store.InsertUserRequest\u003cbr/\u003erecords user request\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Store.InsertTrajectory\u003cbr/\u003ecreates trajectory\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Store.InsertEvent\u003cbr/\u003erecords initial event\"]\n        2f[\"2f: Trajectory.InsertTrajectory\u003cbr/\u003epersists to SQLite\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph DupHandle[\"Duplicate Handling\"]\n        4a[\"4a: isDuplicate flag detected\u003cbr/\u003ebranches to handler\"]\n        4c[\"4c: HandleDuplicate\u003cbr/\u003ewaits for completion\"]\n        4d[\"4d: WaitForCompletion\u003cbr/\u003epolls job state\"]\n        4e[\"4e: Load result from job\u003cbr/\u003ereads result.json\"]\n        4f[\"4f: HandleResult\u003cbr/\u003eprocesses cached result\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Execution[\"Execution Path\"]\n        5a[\"5a: ExecuteSync\u003cbr/\u003emain execution entry\"]\n        5b[\"5b: ExecutePreparedSkill\u003cbr/\u003eexecutes via store\"]\n        5d[\"5d: runSkill\u003cbr/\u003einvokes skill binary\"]\n        5e[\"5e: HandleResult\u003cbr/\u003eprocesses execution result\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph ResultCapture[\"Result Capture \u0026 Trajectory Update\"]\n        5g[\"5g: CaptureResult\u003cbr/\u003ecaptures in trajectory\"]\n        6a[\"6a: Parse envelope\u003cbr/\u003eextracts status and data\"]\n        6d[\"6d: InsertEvent\u003cbr/\u003erecords result event\"]\n        6f[\"6f: UpdateTrajectory\u003cbr/\u003eupdates status\"]\n        6g[\"6g: Trajectory.UpdateTrajectory\u003cbr/\u003epersists to SQLite\"]\n    end\n    \n    1a --\u003e|invokes| 1b\n    1b --\u003e|delegates| 1c\n    1c --\u003e|forwards| 1d\n    1d --\u003e|calls when dedupe enabled| 1e\n    1e --\u003e|queries| 1f\n    1f --\u003e|inserts if not found| 1g\n    \n    1d --\u003e|computes| 3a\n    3a --\u003e|calls| 3b\n    3b --\u003e|marshals| 3c\n    3c --\u003e|hashes input| 3d\n    3d --\u003e|combines| 3e\n    \n    1b --\u003e|initiates in parallel| 2a\n    2a --\u003e|opens| 2b\n    2b --\u003e|records| 2c\n    2c --\u003e|creates| 2d\n    2d --\u003e|records| 2e\n    2e --\u003e|persists| 2f\n    \n    1e --\u003e|returns duplicate flag| 4a\n    4a --\u003e|waits for| 4c\n    4c --\u003e|polls| 4d\n    4d --\u003e|loads| 4e\n    4e --\u003e|processes| 4f\n    \n    1d --\u003e|branches to execution| 5a\n    5a --\u003e|executes| 5b\n    5b --\u003e|invokes| 5d\n    5a --\u003e|processes result| 5e\n    \n    5e --\u003e|captures in trajectory| 5g\n    5g --\u003e|parses| 6a\n    6a --\u003e|records event| 6d\n    6a --\u003e|updates status| 6f\n    6f --\u003e|persists| 6g\n    \n    style CLI fill:#a5d8ff\n    style JobPrep fill:#fcc2d7\n    style JobDedupe fill:#fcc2d7\n    style HashComp fill:#ffec99\n    style TrajInit fill:#99e9f2\n    style DupHandle fill:#b2f2bb\n    style Execution fill:#d0bfff\n    style ResultCapture fill:#ffd8a8"
}